================ fcb049e
fcb049e P2-AR-0041: one P2-ADJ-0002 mechanism (WS-3 x WS-8 reconciliation)

WS-3 (trust t2-binding --provision <bundle>, per-key authorisations under authorities/<id>/, t2-v2
seals, reseal) and WS-8 (trust bind, a versioned authority document with active/retired keys and an
optional machine list, srr::binding::keyring, key installed over t2's machine key) each implemented
P2-ADJ-0002. Unified into one role (t2-binding), one document format (WS-8's versioned
t2-binding-authority), one provisioning command (gov trust bind), one keyring API
(srr::binding::keyring / keyring_at / held_keys), consumed by t2.rs sealing and verification:

- srr/binding.rs: binding never replaces or destroys t2's machine key; keys live in keyring/ (0600,
  dir 0700); result reports action/sealing; keyring() also refuses a machine the authority does not
  list; repository-content refusal also covers the enclosing governed project (WS-3's check);
  status() removed (one status, t2::binding_status).
- t2.rs: provisioned-scope seal = t2-v2 over authority, key id, machine, operation, time, content;
  honoured only when the key is held and the authority verifies NOW and lists it (ACTIVE|RETIRED);
  revoked (absent) keys, an authority that no longer verifies (root succession, expiry, alteration)
  -> UNAUTHORISED; a bound machine does not honour its own machine-scope seals (WS-8 property) and
  re-seals what it sealed while provisioned with gov trust reseal (WS-3 property). WS-3's bundle,
  authorities/ store, second verifier and provision_authority removed.
- CLI/G0: TrustCmd::T2Binding removed; TrustCmd::Reseal ('trust reseal', L4 reseal_t2_bindings;
  '--dry-run' Read); 'trust status' carries the one t2_binding report.
- ws03_r3: converged on the one harness (suite root + suite owner's authority, clone_to_machine,
  foreign_owner) and the unified command/format; the seal is still re-derived independently from its
  documentation; every asserted property kept (typed codes follow the kept command).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>


