================ f1cb985
f1cb985 P2-AR-0041: one availability host API (WS-2 x WS-5 x WS-8); research lifecycle authority (IP-R3-WS03-4)

Every host converges on WS-2's scheduler API (Request/admit/confirm_remedy/guard/subjects_reach):
- tasks::guard_work (create, claim): control::guard_write_host (kernel trust, break-glass, emergency
  controls) + scheduler::admit with the task's subjects — id, record path, declared inputs, feature,
  dependencies, allowed paths (verification::close_subjects; IP-R3-WS02-03) — and its declared
  remedies; a subject-scoped block leaves independent claims available at the host too.
- WS-5's 'work that remedies a block stays available' expressed in WS-2's catalogue: task.create and
  task.claim join WORK_REMEDIES/ALL_REMEDIES as DECLARED_REMEDY_OPS — admitted as a block's remedy
  only when the work declares the block's check (task remedies) AND its subjects reach the block's
  (the conjunction of both builders' conditions; WS-2's own guard doc names 'creating, claiming ...
  the repairing task' as allowed non-committing remedies). Request/Admission carry 'remedies'.
- control::GOVERNED_WORK_OPS drops 'cit propose' (IP-R3-WS02-01): its host guards it with paths.
- update::apply_update_opts (IP-R3-WS02-02 / IP-R3-WS08-4): entry_guard = scheduler::admit with
  catalogue::ops::UPDATE_SUBJECTS (non-remediable blocks refuse at entry, typed, with the rule);
  scheduler::confirm_remedy before commit (HEALTH_REMEDY_INCOMPLETE rolls the transaction back);
  update_can_remedy becomes the catalogue's declaration; WS-8's parallel partition removed.
- cit::guard_paths keeps a file-path target (IP-R3-WS02-04).
- scheduler::with_record_aliases never adds an empty id/path: a record that does not parse loads
  with an empty id, and the empty alias glob-matched every path, so its D023/schema block was 'reached'
  by (and admitted as remedied by) any update — found by ws08_r3's entry-guard test after the
  convergence; unit test added.
- IP-R3-WS03-4: AUTHORITY_POLICY declares record_research_evidence: L1; lifecycle::RECORD_AUTHORITY
  and the twelve research/experiment/data write labels in COMMAND_GUARDS use it (kept equal by
  WS-10's unit test).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>


