================ 22d43ce
22d43ce P2-AR-0041: remaining routed integration points (WS-2, WS-3, WS-4, WS-5, WS-6, WS-8, WS-9)

- IP-R3-WS02-07: memory::integrity accepts TESTS from work to work (a revalidation task re-tests the
  completed work it names; records.rs revalidates -> TESTS), narrowly (other sources still cannot
  'test' work); proven by integration_r3::a_cit_invalidating_done_work_leaves_graph_integrity_and_d015_clean.
- R3-WS5-7 / IP-R3-WS02-08: recovery::recover writes evidence/discoveries/unresolved items as strings
  (the report schema; exact JSON text) and seals the report (IP-R3-WS04-04).
- IP-R3-WS02-09: misplaced_os_state findings are medium now that every BC-P2-31 writer moved.
- IP-R3-WS03-5 / IP-R3-WS08-8 / IP-R3-WS04-07: gov release record wired (WS-8's writer, WS-4's record
  type, WS-3's G0 class record_release; the writer requires that class).
- R3-WS5-4: CLI task show -> tasks::show (record + DAG evaluation, staleness, generation source).
- R3-WS5-1 review: the post-command work generation does not run after any guard refusal
  (HEALTH_HARD_BLOCK, kernel-trust and below-floor refusals, besides the pre-dispatch ones).
- IP-R3-WS09-3: harness tree_hash excludes .governance-state/** by default.
- IP-R3-WS08-6: M-4.1.5-4.1.6 description states it is the operative 4.1.5 -> 4.1.6 migration.
- ws03_r3 gate/task test: the 'unsealed task record' is made explicitly (gov task create now seals).
- Docs (IP-R3-WS08-2, P2-ADJ-0002 unification): trust bind / trust status / trust reseal; the removed
  trust t2-binding surface no longer documented; update snapshots at .governance-state/update.

